# SABOTAGE: T137 (ADR-043 §6.1 / §3.2) gate sabotage — grant-verdict truthiness on the AI
# egress binding path. Weakens `Samen.Api.PiiResolution.resolve_egress/7` back to accepting ANY
# truthy grant-checker verdict (drops the `=== true` literal-true strictness the chokepoint's
# history check + `granted?/2` already require). A host-injected grant checker is adversarial
# input: one returning a TRUTHY-NON-true verdict (`:yes`, a map, a PID, …) would then admit
# grant-plaintext into the egress payload by accident — an INV-7 no-PII-egress breach. This
# flips the NAMED T137 verbs test, whose grant checker returns `:yes`: with the strictness gone,
# the vault-routed canary egresses to the fake provider recording (its `refute recorded =~
# @canary` fails, and its `assert recorded =~ mask()` positive control loses the mask). The
# `true`-returning positive control in the same file still passes (the sabotage only re-opens
# the truthy-non-true hole), so the flip is non-vacuous. Reverts byte-exact.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/verbs_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: TRUTHY-NON-true grant verdict
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/api/pii_resolution.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/api/pii_resolution.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/api/pii_resolution.ex
